{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"LOOP ITERATION — J8 round 3: 2 blocks, both the SAME finding, and it is my recurring failure mode for\nthe FIFTH time. The ACs still said '6 declared vs 15 called' while the Context section of the same plan\nhad already been corrected to 21. The reviewer put it exactly right: the AC section is 'the\nauthoritative checklist an implementer will execute against'.\n\nThe pattern, now unmistakable: I correct an analysis section and leave the criteria stale, or correct\nthe criteria and leave Scope stale. Five instances — J9's Scope file list (twice), J9's observability\nmechanism, J8's Approach omissions, and now J8's AC figure. Every one caught by the gate, none by me.\n\nFixed, and the AC now also carries WHY 21 rather than 15: a call-form-only AST scan misses six members\nthe reconciler reaches for as VALUES, e.g. _call_with_retry(client.delete_issue_link, link_id). That\nexplanation belongs in the ADR itself — it is the reason any audit of this seam must match attribute\nACCESS rather than invocation, and it is the specific mistake that produced a wrong member count twice."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785508129525640001,"uuid":"14895c40-7c15-4f3b-880e-1da03e7f2384"}